---
export const prerender = false;

import TopNav from "../../components/TopNav.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import {
  formatByteSize,
  getReportDownloads,
  reportDownloadPath,
} from "../../lib/reportDownloads";

const reportSlug = "nh-education-aid-per-pupil";
const categoryLabels = new Map([
  ["district-adequacy", "District adequacy"],
  ["charter-schools", "Charter schools"],
  ["education-freedom-accounts", "Education Freedom Accounts"],
]);

let reportDownloads = [];

try {
  reportDownloads = await getReportDownloads(reportSlug);
} catch (error) {
  console.error(JSON.stringify({
    event: "education_report_downloads_unavailable",
    message: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),
  }));
}

const bundleDownloads = reportDownloads.filter(
  (download) => download.category === "source-bundle",
);
const sourceDownloadGroups = Array.from(categoryLabels, ([category, label]) => ({
  category,
  label,
  downloads: reportDownloads.filter((download) => download.category === category),
})).filter((group) => group.downloads.length > 0);
const sourceFileCount = sourceDownloadGroups.reduce(
  (total, group) => total + group.downloads.length,
  0,
);
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="description" content="A source-based review of New Hampshire state education aid per pupil, including district aid, SWEPT, charter schools, and Education Freedom Accounts.">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/NH%20DB%20Logo.svg">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/NH%20DB%20Logo.svg">
    <title>One Trend Line, Three Calculations — NH Education Aid Per Pupil</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <TopNav />
<main>
<header class="education-report-hero" id="top">
<div class="shell hero-grid">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">New Hampshire education funding</p>
<h1>One trend line. At least three different calculations.</h1>
<p class="dek">The legislator’s figures are not a consistent measure of state aid paid per pupil. Earlier years resemble a formula cost. FY2026 and FY2027 include SWEPT. Switching methods creates most of the apparent jump.</p>
<nav class="jump-links" aria-label="Jump to report section">
<a href="#finding">The finding</a>
<a href="#hypothesis">Likely formulas</a>
<a href="#programs">Programs</a>
<a href="#sources">Fact-check</a>
</nav>
</div>
<aside class="hero-verdict" aria-label="Report conclusion">
<span class="verdict-label">Plain-language conclusion</span>
<strong>Education funding rose. The posted 10-year comparison still is not apples to apples.</strong>
<span>We can reproduce the recent numbers only by changing the formula between years.</span>
</aside>
</div>
</header>
<section class="shell section" id="finding" aria-labelledby="finding-heading">
<div class="section-heading">
<p class="section-number">01</p>
<div>
<h2 id="finding-heading">The claimed jump mostly disappears when the method stays the same</h2>
<p>The post says aid rose from $5,251 to $7,100 in one year. That comparison changes what is counted.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="finding-grid">
<article class="finding-card bad-card">
<span>Posted comparison</span>
<strong>$5,251 → $7,100</strong>
<b>+$1,849 · +35.2%</b>
<p>FY2025 and FY2026 appear to use different numerators.</p>
</article>
<article class="finding-card good-card">
<span>Same gross-district method</span>
<strong>$6,870 → $7,096</strong>
<b>+$226 · +3.3%</b>
<p>District grant plus SWEPT, divided by district ADM, in both years.</p>
</article>
<article class="finding-card neutral-card">
<span>Actual state grant, no SWEPT</span>
<strong>$4,518 → $4,707</strong>
<b>+$188 · +4.2%</b>
<p>District adequacy grant paid, excluding the locally raised SWEPT amount.</p>
</article>
</div>
<div class="formula-walkthrough" aria-label="FY2025 and FY2026 calculation walkthrough">
<article>
<span class="formula-year">FY2025 posted: $5,251</span>
<h3>Closest match: calculated cost</h3>
<div class="big-equation">
<b>$817.9m</b>
<i>÷</i>
<b>154,925</b>
<i>=</i>
<strong>$5,279</strong>
</div>
<p>Calculated adequate-education cost ÷ district ADM. The $28 difference could reflect rounding or an earlier estimate.</p>
</article>
<div class="method-switch" aria-hidden="true">
<span>method changes</span>
</div>
<article>
<span class="formula-year">FY2026 posted: $7,100</span>
<h3>Near-exact match: grant plus SWEPT</h3>
<div class="big-equation">
<b>$716.1m + $363.5m</b>
<i>÷</i>
<b>152,140</b>
<i>=</i>
<strong>$7,096</strong>
</div>
<p>Actual district grant plus SWEPT ÷ district ADM. FY2027 reproduces the same way: approximately $7,133.</p>
</article>
</div>
<aside class="plain-callout">
<strong>What is misleading?</strong>
<p>The post compares a cost estimate in one year with a larger, SWEPT-inclusive funding measure in the next year and labels both “state aid per pupil.”</p>
</aside>
</section>
<section class="definitions-band" aria-labelledby="definitions-heading">
<div class="shell section">
<div class="section-heading light-heading">
<p class="section-number">02</p>
<div>
<h2 id="definitions-heading">Three similar labels that mean different things</h2>
<p>Using FY2025, here is how the state report moves from a formula cost to the final displayed grant.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="definition-grid">
<article>
<span>1</span>
<h3>Calculated cost</h3>
<strong>$817.9m</strong>
<p>Base aid plus additions for free/reduced-price eligibility, special education, English learners, and home education. This is a formula estimate—not the state check.</p>
</article>
<article>
<span>2</span>
<h3>Adequacy grant paid</h3>
<strong>$700.0m</strong>
<p>Calculated town by town: cost minus SWEPT, plus extraordinary-needs and hold-harmless grants. This is the district grant excluding SWEPT.</p>
</article>
<article>
<span>3</span>
<h3>Final grant including SWEPT</h3>
<strong>$1.064b</strong>
<p>The $700.0 million adequacy grant plus $364.4 million of SWEPT. SWEPT is locally raised property-tax revenue.</p>
</article>
</div>
<div class="fy25-stack">
<div>
<span>Calculated cost</span>
<b>$817.9m</b>
</div>
<i>−</i>
<div>
<span>SWEPT</span>
<b>$364.4m</b>
</div>
<i>+</i>
<div>
<span>Extraordinary needs</span>
<b>$158.7m</b>
</div>
<i>→</i>
<div>
<span>Town-level preliminary grants</span>
<b>$640.6m</b>
</div>
<i>+</i>
<div>
<span>Hold harmless</span>
<b>$59.4m</b>
</div>
<i>=</i>
<div class="stack-result">
<span>Adequacy grant</span>
<b>$700.0m</b>
</div>
</div>
<p class="formula-note">The statewide numbers do not reproduce by simple subtraction because the formula is applied municipality by municipality before the results are added.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="shell section" id="hypothesis" aria-labelledby="hypothesis-heading">
